$DATUM RCM product 14{5} A round-bottomed flask was fitted with a magnetic
stirring bar and charged with 4{21} (100mg, 0:24mmol), dry CH2Cl2 (24
mL), Grubbs II (100 mg, 0:024 mmol) and the mixture was stirred at rt
overnight. The mixture was concentrated in vacuo and the residue was
purified by flash column chromatography (EtOAc:heptane 1:2). The title
compound as a brown oil (60mg, 80%). Purity: 93%. RP-HPLC: R t = 7:10min,
IR (neat) cm-1: 3377, 3060, 3030, 2929, 2853, 2255, 1630, 1495, 1446,
1411, 1382, 1236, 1153, 1054, 1025, 1003, 697; 1H NMR (300MHz, DMSO-d 6)
δ 7.58-7.47 (m, 2H), 7.47-7.28 (m, 4H), 7.23-7.10 (m, 2H), 6.93-6.85 (m,
2H), 6.06 (d, J = 9:8Hz, 1H), 5.88-5.76 (m, 1H), 4.58 (d, J = 18:4Hz,
1H), 4.23 (t, J = 5:4Hz, 1H), 3.97 (s, 2H), 3.83 (dd, J = 19; 1:9Hz, 1H),
3.29 (t, J = 5:8Hz, 2H), 2.98 (d, J = 4:6 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (75 MHz,
DMSO-d 6) δ 171.3, 136.7, 136.6, 129.0, 128.5, 128.2, 128.1, 127.5,
127.4, 127.3, 126.2, 123.5, 123.3, 63.0, 59.1, 58.2, 36.3; UPLC-MS (ESI)
m/z: calcd for C19H20N2O2 [M+H]+ 309.2, found 309.2.
